# Local-only on this M4 Air

Compute stays on this MacBook Air (M4, 16 GB unified memory, 256 GB SSD). Document text, prompts, and the index stay on disk. The one network step is `ldi setup`, which downloads weights.

- Runtime is MLX. `ldi ask` and `ldi probe` set the Hugging Face hub offline before loading weights.
- The default path is a 3B 4-bit first run, then a 7B 4-bit model. `1b` is the allowlisted Granite 4.0 1B 4-bit model. Its catalog cap is 1280 MB from a measured 1.1 GB Metal peak, and it stays at or below the 2 GB ceiling. `bge` is the allowlisted BGE Small English v1.5 8-bit embedding, capped at 512 MB. `ocr` is the allowlisted PaddleOCR-VL 1.6 8-bit model, capped at 2 GB, in its own environment. One model at a time. The embedding loads, encodes, and unloads before a chat model loads. The OCR model loads only while the chat model is unloaded. Do not add 14B, 32B, or an embedding model that stays resident beside the chat model.
- Retrieval is SQLite full text, so a question loads one model.
- Before a download, free space after the download stays at or above 25 GB.
- Load only when memory pressure is green or yellow and reclaimable memory covers the Metal cap (512 MB for BGE, 1280 MB for 1B, 2 GB for OCR, 4 GB for 3B, 7 GB for 7B). A model whose cap is at or below 2 GB may load while swap is in use. Red pressure means the model stays unloaded.
- Cap Metal with `mx.metal.set_memory_limit`. Keep `max_kv_size` small. A warm chassis is the chip throttling; leave that alone.
- `ldi search` must keep working with the model unloaded. Text ingest must keep working with the OCR model unloaded. A scanned page may start the OCR process, which exits before a chat model loads.

The machine brief is in `AGENTS.md`. Re-check with `ldi status` before loading weights.
